# React & TypeScript

## Structure

- `src/components/ui/` — primitives (Button, Input, Dialog…).
- `src/components/` / `portfolio/` — feature UI; `src/pages/` — routes; `src/hooks/`, `src/lib/`, `src/types/`, `src/data/`.
- One main export per file. Split when a file gains a second responsibility (prefer clarity over a hard line count).
- Co-locate small private pieces next to the feature rather than premature globals.

## Components

- Typed props (`interface` / `type`); extend native element props when wrapping HTML.
- Keep JSX declarative: heavy formatting/logic → helpers or hooks in `src/lib` / `src/hooks`.
- Data/business logic out of pure presentational leaves when it clarifies testing and reuse.

## Forms & a11y

- Real `<label htmlFor>`; never placeholder-only labels.
- Invalid: `aria-invalid` + `aria-describedby` helper text; set `autocomplete` / `inputmode` where useful.
- Validate submits with Zod when adding or changing forms.
- Loading: skeletons that match final layout size (`animate-pulse` + muted bg).
